.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH GENEEXPRESSION 1 2000-1月 "strain_genes" "strain_genes"
.SH NAME
strain_genes \- Get the gene id list of one strain from the genome gene table.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIstrain_genes(\fBgenomes\fR as any, 
\fBstrain\fR as string, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Get the gene id list of one strain from the genome gene table.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBgenomes\fB \fR\- 
 The genome gene table: a dataframe with the \fBstrain\fR/\fBgene_id\fR columns, or a
 tuple list in the format of \fBlist(strain_id = c(gene_id, ...))\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBstrain\fB \fR\- The target strain genome id.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- The R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
A character vector of the gene id that belongs to the given strain, or an empty
 vector when the strain is not found in the genome table.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
The per-strain matrix that generated by \fBdecompose_community\fR keeps all of the
 gene rows of the union matrix for the row alignment, so this api is usually used
 with the \fBfilter\fR api for extract the genes of one strain before the downstream
 analysis(example as the GSVA pathway scoring):
 
\fBr
 let genes = geneExpression::strain_genes(genomes, "Comamonas sp. Y1");
 let y1 = geneExpression::filter(decomposed$"Comamonas sp. Y1", geneId = genes);
 \fR`
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
geneExpression
.SH FILES
.PP
phenotype_kit.dll
.PP
